### Error cases — proving the API rejects bad input cleanly

@host = {{host}}

### Missing required fields -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "nocreds" }

### Malformed JSON -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ not valid json

### Invalid database name (must be [a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_-]{0,62}) -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "bad name;drop", "username": "u", "password": "p" }

### Unknown engine -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/cassandra/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "mydb", "username": "u", "password": "p" }

### Duplicate name -> 409
# Run 02-provision.http first so {{dbName}} already exists.
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "{{dbName}}", "username": "u", "password": "p" }

### Lifecycle on a non-existent database -> 404
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "ghost" }

### Lifecycle with no name -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/stop
Content-Type: application/json

{}
